    5. Decide total marker count M (3-11). Allocate markers to regions ensuring one region gets strictly the most (the winner), at least 2 regions get >=1 marker, and no ties for first place.
    6. For each region, place its allocated markers at random interior cells (not on grid border, not 4-adjacent to another marker). Replace those cells with the marker color.
    7. The output is [[winner_region_color]].
